# Vite's own convention: loaded automatically by `vite build`'s default production mode, no `--mode`
# flag needed. Committed, not gitignored - none of these values are secrets. The public API origin,
# the public Keycloak issuer URL and the OIDC client id are all meant to be visible to any browser
# that loads this bundle; the client id is public by design (`adr/0023`), because PKCE proves
# possession rather than a client secret a shipped bundle could keep confidential anyway.
#
# **This file's absence was a real defect** (#32, 2026-09-02): `ci.yml`'s publish job passes no
# `VITE_*` build arg on purpose - copied from `ago-console`, where that is correct *because* it has
# this file. Without it `src/config.ts`'s `required(...)` throws on first paint, and the image
# published at `3bf1105` could not boot at all. The `build-test` job passes `.invalid` placeholders
# explicitly, which is why the build always succeeded and nothing caught it.
#
# The hostname below is `20-20`'s proposal and was not yet in DNS when this was written. If it
# changes, this file changes with it - and so do the Gateway route, the certificate's SAN list and
# the Keycloak client's redirect URIs.

VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://calendar.reserve-me.ru
VITE_KEYCLOAK_AUTHORITY=https://auth.reserve-me.ru/realms/ago-chat
VITE_KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID=ago-calendar-console
